// Isolates the question "does substitution work when a call is reached
// THROUGH a dictionary rather than named at the call site" on its own,
// with no second impl and no direct call site to muddy it. The only
// thing knowable about an abstract T, at the generic's own single
// compilation (Sec 7.1: compiled once), is the trait member's OWN
// declared row -- there is no concrete callee name to substitute by, so
// substitution must resolve through the trait's declared ceiling
// instead. `total` declares exactly that ceiling. Expect: accept.
//
// Paired with bad_generic_dictionary_undeclared.exsc: an identical file
// with the one declared row removed. If the checker's dictionary-call
// handling is not vacuous, that mutation must flip the verdict.

interfacies Summable {
    functio combine(self, other: f32) -> f32 poscit alloc
}

publica functio total<T: Summable>(a: T, b: f32) -> f32 poscit alloc {
    redde a.combine(b);
}
